Penny Goblin stores the household ledger on your devices. It does not require a
hosted Penny Goblin account, and this website is separate from the application.

# Scanning and models

Android's text recognition runs on-device. Optional local models can extract
receipt fields on your phone or desktop. If you choose a paired desktop scan,
the receipt image is sent to that authenticated desktop over the encrypted
connection. Model files are downloaded separately from their configured source.

# Pairing and synchronization

Pairing authenticates your desktop and pins its TLS certificate. Your devices
must be reachable over a local network or your configured Tailscale connection.
Treat pairing links and QR codes as private. Secure access to your devices and
keep backups of the ledger and receipt evidence.

# Optional online research

Desktop category research sends merchant names and country context to online
search and visits relevant sources. Payment amounts, accounts and receipt images
are not included in those searches. Search providers and visited websites may
process network metadata under their own policies.

Research is optional. Blocked or uncertain results can stay uncategorized.
The model does not save category changes: you review the evidence and explicitly
apply selected suggestions.

# This website

This static website has no analytics scripts, tracking pixels, external fonts or
account forms. It is hosted by GitHub Pages, whose infrastructure processes web
requests under GitHub's policies. Links to GitHub or other services follow those
services' policies. Illustrations use fictional example payments, not a real ledger.

# Development limits

Penny Goblin is an early development project. OCR and models can misread images
or suggest a wrong category. Review totals, dates and merchants before saving.
CI builds are development artifacts, not audited financial software or a promise
of support for every device and Linux distribution.
